00:29:49,541 --> 00:29:52,540
attributed with mythical qualities, and it eventually

511
00:29:52,541 --> 00:29:56,780
made its way to Europe through trade routes.

512
00:29:56,781 --> 00:29:59,420
Diamonds are crystals of pure carbon.

513
00:29:59,520 --> 00:30:01,880
Each carbon atom is tightly linked

514
00:30:01,980 --> 00:30:07,420
by short covalent bonds, which are the strongest atomic bond,

515
00:30:07,520 --> 00:30:09,820
and centered between four other carbon atoms

516
00:30:09,920 --> 00:30:13,800
in a compact three-dimensional array.

517
00:30:13,900 --> 00:30:18,860
This tight cube arrangement is what makes diamonds so strong.

518
00:30:18,960 --> 00:30:21,940
Diamonds crystallize deep in the Earth's metal

519
00:30:22,040 --> 00:30:25,740
and are brought to the surface by volcanic eruptions,

520
00:30:25,741 --> 00:30:28,940
where they are found today in what is called a kimberlite

521
00:30:29,040 --> 00:30:33,440
pipe, where the diamonds are embedded in the kimberlite.

522
00:30:33,540 --> 00:30:36,380
There were less than 35 operational kimberlite mines

523
00:30:36,480 --> 00:30:37,880
throughout the world.

524
00:30:37,980 --> 00:30:42,220
They are located in North America, Asia,

525
00:30:42,320 --> 00:30:45,560
Australia, and Africa.

526
00:30:45,660 --> 00:30:47,500
This is from southern Africa.

527
00:30:47,600 --> 00:30:51,260
This is a diamond crystal in a piece of kimberlite ore.

528
00:30:51,360 --> 00:30:54,940
It's the typical way diamonds are found in nature today.

529
00:30:54,941 --> 00:30:57,580
These are two natural diamond crystals.

530
00:30:57,680 --> 00:30:59,280
Diamonds, when they're found in the earth,

531
00:30:59,380 --> 00:31:01,740
have this typical octahedral shape,

532
00:31:01,840 --> 00:31:06,980
which you can think of as two pyramids joined at the base.

533
00:31:07,080 --> 00:31:09,280
Although revered for its natural beauty,

534
00:31:09,380 --> 00:31:11,700
diamond is also venerated in applications

535
00:31:11,800 --> 00:31:13,400
that aren't so pretty.

536
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:20,840
Diamond cuts concrete, stone, marble, and tile.

537
00:31:20,940 --> 00:31:23,340
In sharp contrast to the jeweler's showroom,

538
00:31:23,341 --> 00:31:27,080
showroom, diamonds have made their mark in the most grueling of industries.

539
00:31:27,081 --> 00:31:36,520
It's the hardest, strongest material known in the world for cutting all types of material.

540
00:31:38,660 --> 00:31:43,200
MK Diamond Products has a full range of industrial diamond enhanced tools.

541
00:31:43,860 --> 00:31:49,599
The use of diamonds in industrial tool probably started over 100 years ago.

542
00:31:49,600 --> 00:31:50,900
When people cut a

543
00:31:50,901 --> 00:31:53,700
There was a gemstone that was diamond chips.

