555
00:32:28,881 --> 00:32:30,880
These contractions, or joints,

556
00:32:30,881 --> 00:32:33,780
prevented cracks that usually occurred because of shrinkage

557
00:32:33,781 --> 00:32:37,320
during the curing process.

558
00:32:37,321 --> 00:32:39,880
They also created an even, durable surface.

559
00:32:43,160 --> 00:32:46,160
Then in the 1950s, a scientific breakthrough

560
00:32:46,161 --> 00:32:48,500
revolutionized the industry.

561
00:32:48,501 --> 00:32:50,700
There's been a long interest among scientists

562
00:32:50,701 --> 00:32:52,540
to grow diamonds in the laboratory,

563
00:32:52,541 --> 00:32:56,200
and this has extended back several hundred years.

564
00:32:56,201 --> 00:32:58,380
Although others had been able to successfully grow

565
00:32:58,381 --> 00:33:00,780
