566
00:33:00,781 --> 00:33:03,440
it was General Electric that found a way to produce them

567
00:33:03,441 --> 00:33:06,020
on a mass scale.

568
00:33:06,021 --> 00:33:08,560
And they were able to create conditions in the laboratory

569
00:33:08,561 --> 00:33:11,260
with pieces of equipment that allowed you

570
00:33:11,261 --> 00:33:14,920
to reach the temperatures and pressures that were required

571
00:33:14,921 --> 00:33:17,700
to grow a diamond crystal in the laboratory

572
00:33:17,701 --> 00:33:22,740
and to be able to do that on a reproducible basis.

573
00:33:22,741 --> 00:33:28,440
This method is called HPHT, or high pressure, high temperature.

574
00:33:28,441 --> 00:33:32,880
Large presses produce extreme pressure and heat.

575
00:33:32,881 --> 00:33:35,960
They reproduce conditions that create natural diamond deep

576
00:33:35,961 --> 00:33:39,220
inside the earth.

577
00:33:39,221 --> 00:33:41,400
These new creations fed a growing market

578
00:33:41,401 --> 00:33:42,860
of industrial applications.

579
00:33:42,861 --> 00:33:48,860
The Eisenhower administration's post-war federal highway program

580
00:33:48,861 --> 00:33:52,860
duplicated the methods used for the Autobahn and created a need

581
00:33:52,861 --> 00:33:54,860
for diamond tools across the nation.

582
00:33:54,861 --> 00:34:00,860
Synthetic diamonds are grown uniformly, so each is very similar.

583
00:34:00,861 --> 00:34:05,860
Natural diamond chips are of various sizes and shapes,

584
00:34:05,861 --> 00:34:07,860
making the cutability less perfect.

