690
00:40:01,041 --> 00:40:06,040
Then in 1907, Dr. Leo Bakeland combined phenol and formaldehyde

691
00:40:06,041 --> 00:40:10,040
under high heat and pressure to create Bakelite.

692
00:40:10,041 --> 00:40:13,040
Although used in industry and consumer products,

693
00:40:13,041 --> 00:40:16,840
products, Bakelite's brittle nature relegated it to a small

694
00:40:16,841 --> 00:40:21,240
number of applications. However, both celluloid and

695
00:40:21,241 --> 00:40:24,880
Bakelite spurred the scientific community to devise better and

696
00:40:24,881 --> 00:40:29,360
more diverse plastics. Improvements in chemical

697
00:40:29,361 --> 00:40:32,800
technology as a result of the First World War led to a

698
00:40:32,801 --> 00:40:39,360
